e('`flow:established,to_server` means only client-to-server data on a completed connection, which stops an attacker triggering alerts with spoofed packets. `http.uri` restricts the match to the decoded URI. Rule sets such as Emerging Threats contain tens of thousands of rules.', '`flow:established,to_server` selects traffic towards the server in a flow the engine considers established. This is connection tracking, not cryptographic peer authentication or a guarantee against forged traffic; midstream handling also depends on configuration. `http.uri` selects the normalized URI buffer. The string match is only a teaching example, not a complete SQL-injection detector.', 'Established state does not authenticate the sender; rule count is unverified.', ['https://docs.suricata.io/en/latest/rules/flow-keywords.html'])
e('Signatures are precise but only catch what someone has already described.', 'Signatures match specified patterns, which can occur in both known and previously unseen attacks, or in benign traffic.', 'Signature precision and attack novelty are not categorical guarantees.')
