e('Any detector with a small false-positive rate, applied to a huge volume of mostly benign events, produces mostly false alarms.', 'Even a small false-positive rate can overwhelm true alerts when malicious events are rare. If prevalence is p, sensitivity is t and the false-positive rate is f, expected alert precision is t × p / (t × p + f × (1 − p)), when the denominator is nonzero.', 'The original universal statement has counterexamples including zero false-positive rate.')
e('> - True alerts:', '> - Expected true alerts:', 'Probabilistic rates imply expected counts.')
