e('A host sending `[S]` to port after port and receiving `[R]` back is a port scan. `[S]` with no reply at all means a firewall is silently dropping.', 'SYNs to many ports can indicate a scan, but may also be authorized diagnostics. A reset indicates active rejection or abort somewhere along the path, possibly by a middlebox. Silence could reflect filtering, loss, an unavailable host or an unseen return path; it does not identify a firewall by itself.', 'Packet observations do not uniquely identify intent or failure location.')
