e('Capturing on a host shows packets before the NIC segments them (TSO) or after it merges them (GRO), so you see "packets" of 30 KB and outbound checksums flagged as wrong. Neither is real on the wire.', 'Depending on the capture hook and enabled offloads, host captures can show large buffers before transmit segmentation or after receive coalescing, and outbound checksums before hardware fills them in. Such apparent errors need not occur on the wire.', 'Offload artifacts depend on capture point and configuration.')
